                l2 = l2.next
            carry, digit = divmod(total, 10)
            tail.next = ListNode(digit)
            tail = tail.next
        return dummy.next
```

**Time/Space:** O(max(m, n)) / O(max(m, n))

**Pitfall:** A final carry needs its own node (e.g. 5 + 5).

**Pattern:** Floyd's cycle detection

**Key insight:** Treat i → nums[i] as a linked list; the duplicate is the cycle entrance.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int findDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        int slow = nums[0], fast = nums[nums[0]];
        while (slow != fast) { slow = nums[slow]; fast = nums[nums[fast]]; }
        slow = 0;
        while (slow != fast) { slow = nums[slow]; fast = nums[fast]; }
        return slow;
    }
}
```

